    "updated_at": "2023-04-12T00:41:03Z",
    "body": "I mean, the replace-before-load behavior is always replacing some unrelated load, right? It's a weird behavior. The approach we've taken so far is to just try to get to interop in this area, not try to do the most sensible thing. (Which IMO would be not having such magic in the first place.)\r\n\r\nRegardless, if you think this is not straightforward, I'll be sure to write some more-extensive tests and double-check with Chromium folks before pushing ahead, then.",
